MP-SPDZ 0.4.3 compatibility for Apple Clang 20 on arm64 macOS.

The PRNG type depends on the protocol template parameter. Newer Clang rejects
the unqualified member-template call instead of accepting it as an extension.
This changes no generated code or protocol behavior; it only makes the
standard-required `template` disambiguator explicit.

--- a/Protocols/ReplicatedInput.hpp
+++ b/Protocols/ReplicatedInput.hpp
@@ -197,10 +197,10 @@ void PrepLessInput<T>::add_mine(vector<T>& target, octetStream& dest,
         auto& G = protocol.shared_prngs[1];
         if (im_in)
             for (auto& x : target)
-                x[1] += G.get<typename T::open_type>();
+                x[1] += G.template get<typename T::open_type>();
         else
             for (auto& x : target)
-                x[1] = G.get<typename T::open_type>();
+                x[1] = G.template get<typename T::open_type>();
     }
 }
